fof_version: '0.1'
type: enemy
id: waiting_one
name: A Waiting One
ruleset:
  modules:
  - id: base
    version: 0.1.0
enemy:
  tier: named
  attack_modifier: 2
  defense_modifier: 1
  armor: none
  techniques:
  - the_task
  special: THE TASK — a Waiting One is doing something, and the MM knows what. Any
    character who takes an action that genuinely advances that task is not a target
    this exchange, and the Waiting One will work around them.
  description: Someone at work. The hands move, the tools are real, and the job
    is being done properly. It is only when you have watched for a while that you
    notice the job was finished a long time ago, and is being done again.
  disposition: Occupied. Violence is an interruption, and it is treated as one.
  first_target: Whoever is between it and the work.
  triggers:
  - Never strikes first, and never strikes anyone who is helping.
  - Becomes immediately and comprehensively dangerous to anyone who damages the
    work.
  morale: Stops when the task is finished, and only then. Nothing else stops it;
    at Resolve 0 it simply cannot continue, which is not the same thing and the
    fiction should say so.
  organization: 'Where people died mid-task: one to four, each on its own job.'
  notes: 'TR breakdown: offense(+2 → 4) + durability(Resolve 4) + armor(none → 0)
    + techniques(1) = 9.'
  negotiation: Wants the work done. Shifts for help. Honours nothing, because it
    is not making agreements — but a party that finishes the job is not opposed
    again.
  resolve: 4
created_at: '2026-08-02T00:00:00+00:00'
last_modified: '2026-08-02T00:00:00+00:00'
